{
  "rationale": "The tests include a full BFS oracle (test_full_bfs_oracle) that computes the correct answer independently, and nine specification‑based checks: output must be an integer not zero; if any a_i equals n the answer must be 1; if all a_i are strictly above or below n the answer must be -1; if both positive and negative differences exist a solution always exists so the answer cannot be -1; etc. Each test is derived directly from the problem statement or from elementary number‑theory facts that guarantee a solution. All tests hold for every correct solution on the given 30 inputs. The weakest test is test_output_not_zero because a zero output is trivially impossible, but it is included for completeness. If one test had to be dropped, it would be test_output_not_zero.",
  "tests": [
    {
      "name": "test_integer_output",
      "source": "def test_integer_output(run, x):
    out = run(x)
    try:
        val = int(out.strip())
    except ValueError:
        assert False, 'Output must be an integer'
    assert val == -1 or val >= 1, 'Output must be -1 or a positive integer'"
    },
    {
      "name": "test_ai_eq_n_implies_one",
      "source": "def test_ai_eq_n_implies_one(run, x):
    lines = x.strip().splitlines()
    n_k = lines[0].split()
    if len(n_k) < 2:
        return
    n = int(n_k[0])
    a_vals = list(map(int, lines[1].split()))
    if any(a == n for a in a_vals):
        out = run(x)
        assert out.strip() == '1', 'When a type equals n, answer must be 1'"
    },
    {
      "name": "test_all_above_n_implies_minus_one",
      "source": "def test_all_above_n_implies_minus_one(run, x):
    lines = x.strip().splitlines()
    n_k = lines[0].split()
    if len(n_k) < 2:
        return
    n = int(n_k[0])
    a_vals = list(map(int, lines[1].split()))
    if all(a > n for a in a_vals) and not any(a == n for a in a_vals):
        out = run(x)
        assert out.strip() == '-1', 'When all a_i > n and none equal n, answer must be -1'"
    },
    {
      "name": "test_all_below_n_implies_minus_one",
      "source": "def test_all_below_n_implies_minus_one(run, x):
    lines = x.strip().splitlines()
    n_k = lines[0].split()
    if len(n_k) < 2:
        return
    n = int(n_k[0])
    a_vals = list(map(int, lines[1].split()))
    if all(a < n for a in a_vals) and not any(a == n for a in a_vals):
        out = run(x)
        assert out.strip() == '-1', 'When all a_i < n and none equal n, answer must be -1'"
    },
    {
      "name": "test_zero_b_not_minus_one",
      "source": "def test_zero_b_not_minus_one(run, x):
    lines = x.strip().splitlines()
    n_k = lines[0].split()
    if len(n_k) < 2:
        return
    n = int(n_k[0])
    a_vals = list(map(int, lines[1].split()))
    if any(a == n for a in a_vals):
        out = run(x)
        assert out.strip() != '-1', 'When a type equals n, answer cannot be -1'"
    },
    {
      "name": "test_both_signs_not_minus_one",
      "source": "def test_both_signs_not_minus_one(run, x):
    lines = x.strip().splitlines()
    n_k = lines[0].split()
    if len(n_k) < 2:
        return
    n = int(n_k[0])
    a_vals = list(map(int, lines[1].split()))
    b_vals = [a - n for a in a_vals]
    has_pos = any(b > 0 for b in b_vals)
    has_neg = any(b < 0 for b in b_vals)
    if has_pos and has_neg:
        out = run(x)
        assert out.strip() != '-1', 'When both positive and negative differences exist, a solution exists, so answer cannot be -1'"
    },
    {
      "name": "test_output_not_zero",
      "source": "def test_output_not_zero(run, x):
    out = run(x)
